.TH MYSTRLEN 1 "September 2026" "libmyutils 1.0" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mystrlen \- calculate the length of a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "int mystrlen(const char *" s ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mystrlen()
function computes the length of the string pointed to by
.I s
by counting characters until a null terminator is reached, excluding the
terminator itself. This is a custom implementation of the standard C
library's
.BR strlen (3)
function, written for educational purposes as part of the libmyutils
library.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of characters in the string, not counting the
terminating null byte.
